      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Reproductive surgery preserves, enhances or restores fertility. The minimal access surgery offers many benefits in relation to open surgery. Robot-assisted laparoscopic surgery is a relatively new technique in the field of gynecological surgery."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "CLINICAL CASE",
          "content": "A 30-year-old female patient, with primary infertility of five years of evolution in who uterine myomatosis of large elements was diagnosed and robot-assisted laparoscopic surgery was indicated."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "The advantages of robot-assisted laparoscopic surgery are: lower blood loss, hospital stay and postoperative pain and faster reinstatement to normal activities, in addition to a promising reproductive outcome for the patient."
        }
      ]},
